issues.body:
### Check for previous/existing GitHub issues

- [x] I have checked for previous/existing GitHub issues

### Description

It's a common pattern to consume AVM modules in your own .bicep files. Most often in my experience, we create our own `pattern` modules, consuming AVM `resource` modules, and more often than not, these `pattern` modules are again deployed using a .bicepparam file. For example a .bicepparam file per environment. 

This becomes very cumbersome when it comes to parameters and parameter naming. Essentially _piping_ parameters up in the template and parameter file chain.

Sure, we have the AVM convention [pmnfr5](https://azure.github.io/Azure-Verified-Modules/specs/bcp/ptn/#id-pmnfr5---category-inputs---parametervariable-naming) for naming parameters, but it's quite labour-intensive to implement properly. 

My suggestion is that `User-defined Types` combined with `@export()` can be used to greatly simplify this. 
We can instead of having _x_ number of `param` statements for a template, we simply have one UDT parameter for the whole template.

Take the following example. 

Of course, in this example, where the modules only expose two simple parameters each, it is not an issue, however, consider if it was the virtualMachine module for example, I think it has 76 parameters. 

So just a very simple deployment of a resource group with a VM can become hugely complex.

What do you all think? 

This could also potentially be solved in Bicep directly, as per suggestion: https://github.com/Azure/bicep/issues/17464

### Current

```bicep
// avm-mock1.bicep
// AVM mock module
param name string
param size string

...
```

```bicep
// avm-mock2.bicep
// AVM mock module
param name string
param sku string

...
```

```bicep
// main.bicep
// Custom pattern module
param mock1Name string
param mock1Size string

param mock2Name string
param mock2Sku string

module mock1 'avm-mock1.bicep' {
  params: {
    name: mock1Name
    size: mock1Size
  }
}

module mock2 'avm-mock2.bicep' {
  params: {
    name: mock2Name
    sku: mock2Sku
  }
}

...
```

### Suggestion

Instead, with the suggestion above, it could look like this:


```bicep
// avm-mock1.bicep
// AVM mock module
param parameters mock1ResourceParametersType

@export()
type mock1ResourceParametersType = {
  param name: string
  param size: string
}

...
```

```bicep
// avm-mock2.bicep
// AVM mock module
param parameters mock2ResourceParametersType

@export()
type mock2ResourceParametersType = {
  param name: string
  param sku: string
}

...
```

```bicep
// main.bicep
// Custom pattern module
import { mock1ResourceParametersType } from 'avm-mock1.bicep'
param mock1Parameters mock1ResourceParametersType

import { mock2ResourceParametersType } from 'avm-mock2.bicep'
param mock2Parameters mock2ResourceParametersType

module mock1 'avm-mock1.bicep' {
  params: {
    ...mock1Parameters
  }
}

module mock2 'avm-mock2.bicep' {
  params: {
    ...mock2Parameters
  }
}

...
```

