### Description

In the current version of the `avm/res/document-db/database-account` bicep shared module, it is seemingly impossible to deploy a Mongo database with `autoscaleSettings.maxThroughput`.

That is, trying to deploy the following: (other params left out for simplicity of demonstration)

```txt
module databaseDeployment 'br/public:avm/res/document-db/database-account:0.18.0' = {
  name: 'databaseDeployment${deploymentPostfix}'
  params: {
    // ..
    mongodbDatabases: [
      {
        name: databaseName
        autoscaleSettings: {
          maxThroughput: databaseMaxThroughput
        }
        // ..
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

The Azure Portal reports the following error:

> Only one of provisionedThroughput and autoScaleMaxThroughput may be specified.

This is (likely) because the [avm/res/document-db/database-account/mongodb-database/main.bicep](https://github.com/Azure/bicep-registry-modules/blob/main/avm/res/document-db/database-account/mongodb-database/main.bicep) sub-template has declared a **default** of `400` for the `throughput` param.

If this is indeed an unintentional bug, I hope it will be fixed very soon. Thanks in advance.

